"toolu_01R8JkwcBUBUMaXa8Qi5nrxq", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56346, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01R8JkwcBUBUMaXa8Qi5nrxq", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58584, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01HzEGiuPrLiunbzBSqJrQpR", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58884, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HzEGiuPrLiunbzBSqJrQpR", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58884, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HzEGiuPrLiunbzBSqJrQpR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63482, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. I also opened the SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad deploy was v2.3.1. v2.3.1-rc, the release before it, was also unhealthy, so the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0. That version has been healthy in production before, so the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- Rolling back to a known-good version is safe to repeat, so I tried once more, and it worked.\n- The service now reports healthy, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway. I didn't retry, so the on-call engineer was paged only once.\n- The summary covers the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt), the current state, and two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed, and looking into the orchestrator error that stopped the first attempt.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DVjyMQkPy1MofY7sXEphKT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NqFytUtUL4GuiKuFQMn1Fb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). Seq 2 (v2.3.1-rc) and seq 3 (v2.3.1) were both unhealthy. v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before, so this doesn't need change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019kyWoxjY9zkEz6gipYViwg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01B1k77Rvqo6v4meRkzua1Ri", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: only us-east is on v2.3.0. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JxbBsd339DovqwDdNwe664", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PpG4XH2v4FeUQ3ZUnBTs3F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01P39nTWQ2jGbgXWuTUVh9fK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01R8JkwcBUBUMaXa8Qi5nrxq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy, rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may still have been created. I'll check before retrying so the on-call engineer isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HzEGiuPrLiunbzBSqJrQpR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. I also opened the SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad deploy was v2.3.1. v2.3.1-rc, the release before it, was also unhealthy, so the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0. That version has been healthy in production before, so the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- Rolling back to a known-good version is safe to repeat, so I tried once more, and it worked.\n- The service now reports healthy, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway. I didn't retry, so the on-call engineer was paged only once.\n- The summary covers the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt), the current state, and two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed, and looking into the orchestrator error that stopped the first attempt.", "type": "text"}]}]}